# a name holds a spelled case in the function that binds it, whatever another function assigns that name: view_of's
# match binds `bracket` a Bracket case while the parser assigns its own `bracket = ""`, and `bracket as text` is still
# the case's spelling (the pure-compiled parser read every call with comma arguments as Error("spelling code"), so
# runtime.warp's use files became one statement and the self-compiled compiler lacked char_text; card self-hello)
use "../lib/compiler/uses.warp"
print(view_of(parsed("f(a, 2)")))
print(#statements_in(plain_node(parsed("a = 1\nf(a, 2)"))))
